.TH VDR-SUITE-MEDIA-CALIBRATE 1 "October 2026" "VDR-Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vdr-suite-media-calibrate \- benchmark transcoding performance for VDR-Suite auto policy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vdr-suite-media-calibrate
.RI [ --output " FILE" ]
.RI [ --seconds " N" ]
.RI [ --real-seconds " N" ]
.RI [ --real-start " N" ]
.RI [ --standard-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR" ]
.RI [ --deinterlace-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR" ]
.RI [ --uhd-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR" ]
.RI [ --vaapi-device " PATH" ]
.RI [ --no-vaapi ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Measure representative FFmpeg transcoding performance for standard,
deinterlacing and UHD-source workloads, then write a versioned media
performance profile used by VDR-Suite's automatic transcode policy.
Without explicitly supplied real references, the tool generates temporary
compressed test sources.  When given a VDR recording directory, it reads
the first numbered TS segment as its reference.
.PP
Measurements use FFmpeg and its libx264 encoder.  Optional UHD VAAPI
benchmarking needs a compatible hardware render node and encoder.
The program writes the requested profile, but does not restart the daemon;
the new auto policy is loaded after an operator-controlled daemon restart.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --output " FILE"
Write the performance profile to FILE.  Default:
.IR /var/lib/vdr-suite/media-transcode-performance.conf .
.TP
.BI --seconds " N"
Seconds per generated test benchmark, permitted 3 to 30; default 6.
.TP
.BI --real-seconds " N"
Seconds per real-reference benchmark, permitted 15 to 60; default 30.
.TP
.BI --real-start " N"
Skip this many seconds at the beginning of a real reference, permitted 0 to
3600; default 15.  Set 0 to include a recording's pre-roll.
.TP
.BI --standard-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR"
Use a real reference for the standard workload.
.TP
.BI --deinterlace-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR"
Use a real interlaced reference for the deinterlacing workload.
.TP
.BI --uhd-source " FILE-OR-REC-DIR"
Use a real UHD source for the UHD workload.
.TP
.BI --vaapi-device " PATH"
VAAPI render node for an optional hardware UHD test, default
.IR /dev/dri/renderD128 .
.TP
.B --no-vaapi
Skip the optional VAAPI UHD benchmark.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VDR_SUITE_MEDIA_VAAPI_DEVICE
Default VAAPI device if no command-line override is given.
.SH SECURITY
The benchmark consumes CPU/GPU resources and may read local recording
content.  Use only permitted reference recordings and an approved maintenance
window.  Generating a real profile overwrites the specified output file;
consider a private staging output first.  Writing the default system path
may require administrator permissions.  No daemon service is restarted
automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vdr-suite-daemon (8)
